        "### Multi-scene story - render every scene\nThe **Scenes Writer** is the Claude Code prompt writer, but it returns `scene_count` consecutive T2VA prompts as a list. The video node renders each one; the preview shows the whole run.\n\nOptional `image` / subject / scenery / object sockets are described into every scene for consistency (T2VA, so nothing becomes <Picture N>).\n\n**Clips land one by one.** The sampler and Save Clip are one node here - **Sampler + Save Clip** - so every scene is sampled, decoded, muxed with its slice of the song and written to `output/` BEFORE the next scene starts sampling. Watch the folder fill up during the run; a crash late in the run keeps everything already saved. (Two separate nodes would sample every scene first and only then start saving.)"
      ],
      "title": "How this works",
      "color": "#222",
      "bgcolor": "#000"
    },
